//
// Phase B runtime seam: the hardware gate.
//
// Runs the multi-ELF runlist legs in runlist_gate.py on a real NPU -- the
// measurement docs/plans/transformer-layer-execution-studies/05a-phase-b-runlist-spike-result.md
// records, and the load-bearing assumption Phases E and F are built on.
//
// This test exists because the driver-run gate for Phase B was
// `ninja check-programming-examples-transformer-layer`, and that suite held only
// the compile-only test (peano, no NPU) and the seam unit tests (host-only).
// Neither touches the NPU, so the phase's central hardware claim reached the
// status board on the session's own say-so. Putting the gate into the suite is
// what makes it driver-verifiable, per
// docs/plans/transformer-layer-execution-studies/14-the-port-loop-harness.md
// ("gates are run by the driver, never self-reported").
//
// Slower than its siblings: four distinct GEMM ELFs are compiled at seq_len 2048
// on a cold cache. `make runlist-gate GATE_ARGS=--run-only` reuses them.
//
// Editing this header: lit scans the WHOLE file for its directives, so naming one
// in prose -- even inside a comment -- registers as a second directive and leaves
// the test UNRESOLVED. Describe them, never spell them out.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_npu2_runlist_gate
// RUN: cd test_npu2_runlist_gate
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile runlist-gate PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s
//
// All four legs, not just the summary line: a leg that never ran prints nothing,
// and a bare check on the final verdict would not notice.
// CHECK: leg A  cross-artifact multi-ELF runlist : PASS
// CHECK: leg A2 xclbin cross-artifact refused    : PASS
// CHECK: leg B  same-artifact aggregation        : PASS
// CHECK: leg C  run_sequence over the layer      : PASS
// CHECK: PHASE B GATE: PASS
